{"id":"x-eff-allocating-fn-calls-only-pure","rules":["EFF-2","STOR-8"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"EFF-2"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A function declaring a write of its cell parameter whose body calls only a pure helper exhibits no such write and is rejected as declared-but-unexhibited. Allocation and release carry no effect entry at all, so no row can be justified by them."}
{"id":"x-arith-iadd-wrap-overflow-to-negative","rules":["OP-1"],"expect":{"exit":0,"kind":"run"},"status":"runnable","doc":"iadd.wrap performs two's-complement wrapping on overflow; i32::MAX + 1 wraps to a negative value, and ordinary control on the computed result maps a mismatch to a nonzero status, verifying the total wrap-mode result."}
