{"id":"x-form-form7-checked-overflow-canonical","rules":["FORM-7","OP-1","SCOPE-3"],"expect":{"exit":0,"kind":"run"},"status":"runnable","doc":"The operands are canonical FORM-7 literals and their checked sum is an expected typed Err handled by ordinary control [FORM-7, OP-1, SCOPE-3]."}
{"id":"x-fn-own-arg-for-ref-param","rules":["FN-1","TYPE-5"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"TYPE-5"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A call passes an own value where the callee signature declares a reference &i32; the caller must conform to the signature exactly [FN-1], a reference being formed only by the & spelling, so the argument-kind mismatch is rejected [TYPE-5]."}
