{"id":"x-integ-give-in-statement-match-rejected","rules":["GIVE-1","OWN-13"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"GIVE-1"},"status":"runnable","reason":"give is legal only inside a let-initializer match arm; the statement match over own Sign moves the scrutinee (OWN-13) but its give arms have no enclosing let-initializer, so the checker cites GIVE-1's checker-scoped restriction. No existing case asserts reject GIVE-1.","doc":"A give placed in a statement match (which acts by effect and yields no value) rather than a let-initializer match is rejected citing GIVE-1, exercising the break-precedent checker-scoped restriction in an enum+match program."}
{"id":"x-integ-checked-overflow-diverts-to-err","rules":["OP-1","GIVE-1","OWN-13","SCOPE-3"],"expect":{"exit":0,"kind":"run"},"status":"runnable","reason":"Exercises the Err arm of a checked op, which most positive cases never take: 2000000000 + 200000000 overflows i32, so iadd.checked returns Err and the give-bound sentinel (0) drives the second compare-match, proving overflow is handled as defined behavior.","doc":"An i32 overflow makes iadd.checked take its Err arm, whose give-bound sentinel then feeds a second compare-match, showing checked arithmetic feeding a match handles overflow as defined behavior rather than UB."}
{"id":"x-struct-construct-read-field","rules":["TYPE-2","GRAM-8","TYPE-5","OP-1"],"expect":{"exit":0,"kind":"run"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A struct is constructed named-in-declared-order [TYPE-2, GRAM-8]; two i32 fields are read [TYPE-5], combined with total wrapping addition, and observed as 3+4==7. The case exercises structure layout, field address calculation, typed load/store, and exits 0."}
