{"id":"fn8-neg-requires-partial-op","rules":["FN-8","OP-2"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"FN-8"},"status":"runnable","doc":"Exact division is proof-required on an input no relation states its way out of, so it stays partial and cannot initialize an erased contract definition [FN-8, OP-2]. It is rejected rather than lowered with a runtime fallback. The exact affine rows are read mathematically in a clause and are admitted; other partial exact rows remain inadmissible."}
{"id":"fn8-pos-requires-affine-row","rules":["FN-8","MSR-5","ENT-3","REF-4","MSR-1"],"expect":{"exit":0,"kind":"run"},"status":"runnable","doc":"The exact affine rows are read mathematically in a clause, so an expansion function states its own size precondition over a measure and a literal factor. A range reference carries its own exact len, equal to its written endpoints, so the caller discharges the requirement from the two formations directly instead of reading descriptor words back and branching on them. The definition binder is renamed from room, which FORM-3 now reserves."}
{"id":"inv1-pos-named-const-atom","rules":["INV-1","ENT-2"],"expect":{"exit":0,"kind":"run"},"status":"runnable","doc":"An integer-typed named const is an affine atom and folds to the one closed value it declares, so a header relation names the declared limit instead of repeating its digits. The const and the result binder are renamed because cap and last are now reserved from every declaration role."}
