{"id":"form3-neg-requires-binding","rules":["FORM-3","FN-8"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"FORM-3"},"status":"runnable","doc":"The new requires grammar word is reserved and cannot be rebound as a parameter or other IDENT declaration."}
{"id":"own1-neg-bare-uniq-copy","rules":["REF-1","EFF-1","OWN-1"],"expect":{"kind":"accept"},"status":"runnable","doc":"VERDICT CHANGED from rejection to acceptance at v0.60: a reference carries no permission marker and is no affine value of its own, so passing a received reference on to a reference parameter is the ordinary forwarding spelling. Whether a callee writes through that path is stated by its effect row, not duplicated on the reference."}
{"id":"fn8-neg-empty-contract","rules":["FN-8"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"FN-8"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A syntactically present but empty contract has no definition, requirement, or ensured relation. FN-8 rejects the empty proof surface rather than silently discarding the block; the separate no-clause case retains define-only coverage."}
