{"id":"type7-neg-match-borrow-expression","rules":["TYPE-7","OWN-13","REF-1"],"expect":{"kind":"accept"},"status":"runnable","doc":"Verdict changed at v0.60: a borrow expression is an atom naming a path, so it is an ordinary reference scrutinee and the match leaves the scrutinee live [OWN-13]. v0.59 demanded that it first be bound and explicitly dereferenced."}
{"id":"type7-neg-match-reference-call","rules":["TYPE-5","TYPE-9","OWN-13","REF-3"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"TYPE-5"},"status":"runnable","doc":"Rejecting rule changed at v0.60: a cell-returning call yields an owned Box temporary rather than the enclosed enum, so the match scrutinee has no enum type [TYPE-5]; references are never returned [REF-3], so the Box is what a finder hands back and holder.inner is the fix [TYPE-9]. v0.59 cited TYPE-7."}
