{"id":"type7-neg-propagate-reference-holder","rules":["ERR-3","OWN-1","REF-1"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"OWN-1"},"status":"runnable","doc":"Propagation is a consuming context [ERR-3], and the place deref(holder) reaches through a reference parameter is not rooted in a live own-mode binding, so OWN-1 owns the refusal rather than TYPE-7."}
{"id":"type7-neg-propagate-box-holder","rules":["ERR-3","TYPE-9"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"ERR-3"},"status":"runnable","doc":"Rejecting rule changed at v0.60: propagation requires an operand of own Result type and a Box is not one [ERR-3]; the enclosed Result is the ordinary field inner [TYPE-9], so the operand is written holder.inner. v0.59 cited TYPE-7 as a missing dereference."}
{"id":"type7-neg-return-box-as-referent","rules":["FN-1","TYPE-9","OWN-1"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"FN-1"},"status":"runnable","doc":"Rejecting rule changed at v0.60: returning a Box where its content type is the declared result is an ordinary return type mismatch [FN-1]; the content is the field inner [TYPE-9], so the fix is move holder.inner, and transferring the cell itself is a distinct affine move. v0.59 cited TYPE-7."}
{"id":"own1-neg-return-through-shared-borrow","rules":["OWN-1","REF-1"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"OWN-1"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A return cannot move an owned struct out of the path a reference names; the place is not rooted in a live own-mode binding of the returning function."}
{"id":"own1-neg-return-borrowed-box","rules":["OWN-1","REF-1"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"OWN-1"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A reference names the cell's path; the cell is affine and owned by the binding that reference reaches, so a return cannot move it out through the reference."}
{"id":"own1-pos-return-affine-contextual-move","rules":["OWN-1","TYPE-7"],"expect":{"kind":"accept"},"status":"runnable","doc":"An own affine struct or cell in return position is moved exactly once without confusing cell transfer with content access."}
{"id":"own1-neg-match-move-through-borrow","rules":["OWN-1","OWN-13","REF-1"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"OWN-1"},"status":"runnable","doc":"CITED RULE CHANGED at v0.60 from the retired OWN-5 to OWN-1: a move requires a place rooted in a live own-mode binding, so it cannot steal the referent a reference names, and the ordinary bare match through the reference leaves the scrutinee live and binds the payload as a reference [OWN-13]."}
{"id":"own13-pos-borrow-affine-payload","rules":["OWN-13","REF-1"],"expect":{"kind":"accept"},"status":"runnable","doc":"Matching an enum through a reference binds an affine struct payload as a reference naming that path, and a field of it is read without transferring ownership."}
{"id":"own5-neg-match-borrow-affine-payload-move","rules":["OWN-1","OWN-13","REF-1"],"expect":{"kind":"reject","rule":"OWN-1"},"status":"runnable","doc":"CITED RULE CHANGED at v0.60 from the retired OWN-5 to OWN-1: a payload binder derived from matching through a reference names the scrutinee path, which is not rooted in a live own-mode binding of this function, so its affine referent cannot be moved out."}
{"id":"own13-pos-uniq-match-payloads","rules":["OWN-13","REF-1","OWN-7","SET-1"],"expect":{"exit":0,"kind":"run"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A payload binder derived from matching through a reference names the scrutinee path extended by its payload step, so it writes that storage while the enum stays live and a second match reads the result back."}
{"id":"own1-pos-match-copy-payload-reuse","rules":["OWN-1","OWN-13"],"expect":{"kind":"accept"},"status":"runnable","doc":"A user-enum match binder receives its concrete tag-only payload type, so repeated nested matches copy it instead of falsely consuming an untyped affine value."}
